course: dictionary
lesson: 15912
title: Unobserved
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unobserved has three parts. Un- means not, observe means to watch or notice, and -ed shows it describes something. So unobserved means not watched or noticed by anyone. Look for the part that is missing: nobody saw it.
explain: «The cat crept across the kitchen, unobserved, and ate the fish from the table.» The clue is crept: a sneaky cat does not want to be seen. Ask yourself: did anyone see? No one did, so unobserved means nobody noticed.
explain: Scientists use the word too. «The comet was unobserved until last night.» In science, unobserved can mean not yet watched or recorded. Safety uses it as well: «Young children should never be left unobserved near water.» Here it means an adult must keep watching them.
fact: Observe means to watch or notice carefully.
fact: Un- at the start of a word means not, so unobserved means not observed.
fact: «Unobserved» means not seen or noticed by anyone.
fact: In science, «unobserved» means not yet watched or recorded.
fact: To check your meaning, swap in «not noticed by anyone». If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
exercise: «The fox slipped into the henhouse, unobserved by the farmer.» What does unobserved mean here? | Covered in mud | *Not seen by anyone | Very hungry | Made of wood
exercise: Scientists wrote, «The comet was unobserved until last night.» What does this tell us? | It was too hot to touch | *It had not yet been watched or recorded | It was very loud | It was seen by a thousand people
exercise: Mum says, «Never leave the baby unobserved in the bath.» What does she mean? | *Stay close and keep watching | Wash the baby's hair quickly | Leave the bath running for an hour | Give the baby a toy to play with and go out
test: «The rare bird nested in the reeds, unobserved for years.» What does unobserved mean here? | Covered in colour | Found by a scientist the same day | Very noisy | *Not seen or noticed by anyone
test: The new plant grew in the forest, ___ by any scientist. Which word fills the gap? | Unkind | Unlocked | Unhappy | *Unobserved
exam: «The toddler wandered off to the pond, unobserved for a moment.» What does this sentence tell you? | The pond was dry | She had a lovely time with the frogs | She went to the shop with Mum | *Nobody saw her go, so it was unsafe
